  "question": {
    "text": "A radioactive sample has an average life of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ms</mi></math>&nbsp;and is decaying. A capacitor of capacitance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math>&nbsp;is first charged and later connected with resistor&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>.</mo></math> If the ratio of the charge on the capacitor to the activity of the radioactive sample is fixed with respect to time then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> should be<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>_______&#937;</mi><mo>.</mo></math>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "150",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ms</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>q</mi><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msub><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mfenced close=\"\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>R</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mfenced></msup></math></p><p>Since <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>q</mi><mi>N</mi></mfrac></math> is constant hence<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>R</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mi>C</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>30</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>200</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>150</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math></p>"
  }
}